# 📖 Lab Notes

## Why Build a Pentesting Lab?

A dedicated lab environment allows offensive security concepts to be practiced safely without affecting production systems or external networks.

## Why Kali Linux?

Kali Linux provides many of the tools commonly used during penetration tests including:

- Nmap
- Metasploit Framework
- Burp Suite
- Hydra
- Netcat
- Wireshark

## Why Metasploitable2?

Metasploitable2 is an intentionally vulnerable Linux virtual machine designed for penetration testing practice and training.

## Why Windows 10?

Many enterprise environments contain Windows systems. Including a Windows workstation helps develop skills associated with system enumeration, credential access, privilege escalation, and detection opportunities.

